    Undecided.

The other libraries the daemon and its clients will link have not
been chosen; README.md lists the open choices (the clipboard client's
route to the display server, the FUSE library, and desktop integration).
When a component comes to link a library, it is recorded in that
component's link-dependency list with its SPDX licence identifier, and
listed here:

  - in this section, if the programs are built against the guest's own
    installed copy of the library and no copy of it is placed in this
    repository or shipped from it; or

  - under "Third-party work carried in this repository", with its
    notices, if any copy of it is vendored, bundled, statically linked
    into a shipped binary, or otherwise shipped.


WHEN AN ENTRY MUST BE ADDED

A build-time dependency creates no notice obligation. A shipped copy
creates one immediately. As soon as any third-party file, fragment,
vendored library or generated artefact derived from third-party work is
placed in this repository, or shipped from it, it must be listed here in
the same commit, with its original notices kept intact. A library that is
statically linked into a distributed binary, or copied onto a release
image so that an offline install works, is a shipped copy.
